{"src":"01-raw/2025-09-25/data/label_141.json","id":6654,"nhanesId":"","bundleName":"","fullName":"EFS Electrolyte Fuel System Orange Splash","brandName":"1st Endurance","brandIpSymbol":"none","upcSku":"0 00000 80003 7","productVersionCode":"36680003.1","pdf":"","thumbnail":"","servingsPerContainer":"25","hasOuterCarton":false,"percentDvFootnote":"Percent Daily Values are based on a 2,000 calorie diet","labelRelationships":[{"type":"Flavor difference","labelId":6652},{"type":"Flavor difference","labelId":81280},{"type":"Flavor difference","labelId":58947},{"type":"Flavor difference","labelId":6653}],"contacts":[{"contactId":2501,"text":null,"types":["Manufacturer"],"contactDetails":{"src":"01-raw/2025-09-25/data/contact_1.json","id":2501,"name":"First Endurance","streetAddress":"P.O. Box 71661","city":"Salt Lake City","state":"Utah","country":null,"zipCode":"84171","phoneNumber":"866-347-7811","email":null,"webAddress":"www.firstendurance.com"}}],"netContents":[{"order":1,"quantity":800,"unit":"Gram(s)","display":"800 Gram(s)"},{"order":2,"quantity":1.8,"unit":"lb","display":"1.8 lb"}],"physicalState":{"langualCode":"E0162","langualCodeDescription":"Powder"},"servingSizes":[{"order":1,"minQuantity":32,"maxQuantity":64,"minDailyServings":1,"maxDailyServings":null,"unit":"Gram(s)","notes":"1 scoop","inSFB":true}],"targetGroups":["Adult (18 - 50 Years)"],"productType":{"langualCode":"A1325","langualCodeDescription":"Other Combinations"},"statements":[{"type":"Suggested/Recommended/Usage/Directions","notes":"Use Directions: Mix one scoop EFS per 12 ounces of water. Consume one serving 15-30 minutes before exercise and take one serving every 30 minutes during exercise. EFS can be mixed up to 2x strength for additional calories and electrolytes. A standard water bottle is 18 ounces and requires 1 1/2 scoops."},{"type":"FDA Disclaimer Statement","notes":"*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"• Next Generation Energy & Endurance Drink\n• The Highest Electrolyte Content Available\n• Prevents Cramping & Dehydration\n• Designed to be Mixed at Varying Strengths"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Electrolyte Fuel System"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Energizing Sports Drink"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Na+ K+ Mg+ Ca+ Cl-\n1160mg Electrolytes"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"NEW & IMPROVED"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"NOW WITH MALIC ACID: The new EFS drink contains 700mg of Malic Acid, which was not found in the previous formula. Malic acid stimulates oxygen consumption by increasing mitochondrial uptake, improving mitochondrial respiration and increasing energy production. Malic acid is essential in the formation of ATP, the body's energy source. Malic acid allows the body to make ATP more efficiently, even under low oxygen, or hypoxic conditions."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Orange Splash"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Presenting the all-new EFS drink mix, completely redesigned with the most advanced endurance technology available. From the latest amino acid technology, superior mineral bioavailability to the addition of Malic Acid, the new EFS formula fuels you with EVERYTHING you need to maximize endurance and performance during exercise.(1, 2) And with the highest electrolyte content available, you can train and race with confidence knowing you don't have to worry about cramping or dehydration(3)."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"References:\n(1) Bassit RA, et. al, Branched-chain amino acid supplementation and the immune response of long-distance athletes. Nutrition. 2002 May;18(5):376-9 \n(2) Jentjens RL. Underwood K. Achten J, Currell K, Mann CH, Jeukendrup AE. Exogenous carbohydrate oxidation rates are elevated after combined carbohydrate sources during exercise in heat. J Appl Physiol. 2006 Mar; 100 (3):807-16.\n(3) Brouns, F., et al. 1992 Rationale for upper limits of electrolyte replacement during exercise. Int J Sport Nutr 2:229-38.\n(4) Chaturvedi, P, et al,. Comparison of calcium absorption from various calcium containing products in healthy human adults: a bioavailability study. KGK Synergize FASEB 2006."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"SUPERIOR MINERAL BIOAVAILABILITY: The new EFS formulas utilizes two unique sources of calcium and magnesium. DiCalcium malate and Dimagnesium malate have superior bioavailability compared to other mineral sources. In a bioavailability study, absorption rates were between 20% and 100% higher using DiCalcium and DiMagnesium malates (4)."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"THE HIGHEST ELECTROLYTE CONTENT AVAILABLE: Clinical research shows endurance athletes require much higher levels of electrolytes than most sports drinks provide to prevent cramping and dehydration(3). The new EFS drinks now contain over 1,160mg of all 5 electrolytes per serving, more than any electrolyte drink on the market."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"THE LATEST AMINO ACID TECHNOLOGY: The Amino Acids in the EFS drinks are AjiPure amino acids, the purest, most-bioavailable source of free-form amino acids available. AjiPure amino acids have purity levels of 99%-100%. This results in faster and more complete absorption."},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"Natural Flavors, No Colors, No Artificial Sweeteners"},{"type":"Seals/Symbols","notes":"AjiPure amino acids\nAjiPure is a registered trademarks of Ajinomoto AminoScience"},{"type":"FDA Statement of Identity","notes":"Energy Drink Supplement"},{"type":"General: Product/Version Code","notes":"36680003.1"}],"claims":[{"langualCode":"P0065","langualCodeD